  "events": [
    {
      "month": "1982-11",
      "title": "The recession reaches a turning point",
      "description": "Economic activity reaches the low point later identified by the NBER. Its official announcement follows in July 1983.",
      "source_ids": ["nber-1982-trough"]
    },
    {
      "month": "1983-03",
      "title": "Missile-defense research sparks debate",
      "description": "President Reagan proposes research into defenses against nuclear missiles. Supporters and critics debate its possibilities and risks.",
      "source_ids": ["reagan-sdi"]
    },
    {
      "month": "1986-01",
      "title": "Challenger is lost",
      "description": "Seven people die when the shuttle breaks apart after launch. NASA pauses shuttle flights and investigates.",
      "source_ids": ["nasa-challenger"]
    }
  ],
  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "The recession grew worse before recovery arrived. Yet every choice finished higher over five years. Coca-Cola led this set, and the international share basket beat the US basket. High interest rates helped cash earn income, while falling rates later helped bond prices. A difficult first year and a strong five-year result can both be true.",
